An archaeologist can't get away with robbing a shop if your rev. is
compiled with the Keystone Kops turned on.  They'll make short work of you
unless you have very good armor, a good weapon and the fighting skills to
handle an endless stream of Kops.  If you insist on robbing the shops
though...

[Spoilers follow]





A chaotic character can rob a shop without the Kops coming after him/her.
The easiest way is to grab the loot and teleport out.  Neutrals and
Lawfuls have to be more crafty.  If you're strong enough, you can kill the
shopkeeper, but your god will be angry with you, so don't pray for a while
until your alignment counter has a chance to reset (by the way, if you
have telepathy, you might lose if if you kill a shopkeeper).  The only other
option is a trained pet.  Bring you pet in and stand in the doorway.  If
the pet drops an item right in front of you, you can pick it up for free.
The first time the pet does this, throw it some food (tripe is best, or a
fresh corpse -- it won't take a food ration unless it's half starved), and
it will, one by one, bring you all the uncursed items in the shop.  If
it's a big shop, you may have to move some items closer to the door.  The
pet may stop or slow down in this activity, in which case it is helpful to
reinforce the training with more food --- but only feed it when it does
what you want, or you'll encourage bad habits.   You need to be very
patient, and it doesn't hurt to have some food for yourself handy.  WHen
you have all the loot you want, or think you can get the pet to retrieve,
you can step inside and resell what youy don't want to the shopkeeper.
This works very well with gems, if you have them identified.   A
shopkeeper won't give you much for an unknown gem, but pays top dollar for
a known one.   If your pet keeps bringing it back, you can rack up many $$.









